 ## Decision
 
-A flow action that throws is dispatched again through the message queue. It is
-retried three times with an exponential delay, starting at 10 seconds. After the
-third failure, the error is logged and the flow continues with the next action.
+A flow action that throws is not retried. The error is logged and the flow
+stops, so later actions never run on a half-processed order. Merchants replay
+the flow from the flow log in the Administration.
 
 ## Consequences
 
-* Flow actions must be idempotent, because they can run more than once.
-* Apps that receive webhooks from flow actions can see the same event twice.
+* Flow actions run at most once, so they no longer need to be idempotent.
+* A short outage of a mail server or webhook target stops the flow until a
+  merchant replays it.
